# Same-origin API proxy.
#
# The browser must never talk to the backend host directly: a public page
# (rtutindahan.netlify.app) that fetches a tailnet address is blocked by
# Chrome's Private Network Access rules, and the backend hostname changes
# whenever the tunnel is re-minted. Proxying through Netlify's edge keeps the
# API on this site's own origin, so CORS and private-address checks drop out
# of the picture entirely.
#
# The upstream is the Tailscale Funnel URL, which is stable across reboots.
/api/*  https://hdtv-commission-accepted-cos.trycloudflare.com/api/:splat  200

# Everything else is the SPA. The app uses hash routing, so no deep-link
# rewrite is required, but this keeps stray paths on index.html.
/*  /index.html  200
